    "text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the total number of 5-digit numbers:**\n   Each digit can be placed in any of the 5 positions, and there are 5 distinct digits. Therefore, the total number of permutations is:\n   \\[\n   5! = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the contribution of each digit to the sum of all numbers:**\n   Each digit will appear in each decimal place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) the same number of times. To find this number, note that each digit will be in each place exactly:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{120}{5} = 24\n   \\]\n   times.\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the contributions of each digit in each place:**\n   - **Units place:**\n     The sum of the digits is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n     \\]\n     Each digit appears 24 times in the units place, so the total contribution from the units place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 24 \\times 10^0 = 24 \\times 24 = 576\n     \\]\n\n   - **Tens place:**\n     The sum of the digits is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n     \\]\n     Each digit appears 24 times in the tens place, so the total contribution from the tens place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 24 \\times 10^1 = 24 \\times 240 = 5760\n     \\]\n\n   - **Hundreds place:**\n     The sum of the digits is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n     \\]\n     Each digit appears 24 times in the hundreds place, so the total contribution from the hundreds place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 24 \\times 10^2 = 24 \\times 2400 = 57600\n     \\]\n\n   - **Thousands place:**\n     The sum of the digits is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n     \\]\n     Each digit appears 24 times in the thousands place, so the total contribution from the thousands place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 24 \\times 10^3 = 24 \\times 24000 = 576000\n     \\]\n\n   - **Ten-thousands place:**\n     The sum of the digits is:\n     \\[\n     1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n     \\]\n     Each digit appears 24 times in the ten-thousands place, so the total contribution from the ten-thousands place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 24 \\times 10^4 = 24 \\times 240000 = 5760000\n     \\]\n\n4. **Sum the contributions from all places:**\n   \\[\n   576 + 5760 + 57600 + 576000 + 5760000 = 6400006\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the average:**\n   The average of all these 5-digit numbers is the total sum divided by the total number of numbers:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6400006}{120} = 53333.38333\\ldots\n   \\]\n\nThus, the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed by using each of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{53333.38333\\ldots}\n\\]",
